// THE SHIPPED DEFAULT of the row_house_couples (2026-11-13, docs/design/home-room-program.md). Compiled
// into the exe (crates/humanity-core/src/embedded_data.rs `shipped_home_design`) and never written by
// the game: a neighbour's plot of this kind is drawn as it (crates/humanity-ship/src/neighbours.rs),
// and a game with no data/homes/row_house_couples.ron of its own starts its home from it. YOUR home is
// data/homes/row_house_couples.ron, which every editor Save rewrites; it starts as a copy of this file WITHOUT
// this paragraph (`own_home_text` drops everything from the first line down to the bare // below).
// To change the default every newcomer gets, edit this file (keeping this paragraph on top) and
// rebuild: data/homes/shipped is in build.rs FINGERPRINT_INPUTS, so a rig refuses an exe built
// before the edit. Then redraw it: `node scripts/draw-homes.js <folder>`.
//
// HumanityOS home design: the ROW HOUSE FOR COUPLES SHARING (2026-11-13, docs/design/home-room-program.md
// section 10), one home of a terrace on Row Street (data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron). A draft for
// developers (data/homes/starts.ron, `dev: true`).
//
// Three couples sharing (the operator, 2026-11-13: "Maybe there's a group of couples living in one
// house"): three double bedrooms, each with its own shower room, around one kitchen and one living
// room. The space standard asks 102 m2 for three bedrooms and six people on two storeys and 11.5 m2
// a double (one at least 2.75 m wide, the rest 2.55 m); England's licensing rule for a shared house
// asks less, 10.22 m2 for two (SI 2018/616), so the standard holds. A couple's own shower room
// means the shared-house rule on shared bathrooms does not apply (SI 2006/373, Schedule 3).
// Plot 7 x 18 m (7 m, not 6.5: the step-free couple's shower room needs 2 x 2 m beside a double 3 m
// wide); house 7 x 12 m, the back 2.5 m one storey under a lid; 150.5 m2 gross; yard 7 x 4 m = 28 m2.
// Ground: hall and stair, the step-free couple's room 4.5 x 3 m with its lobby 2.5 x 2 m and shower
// room 2 x 2 m at the front, utility 2.5 x 2 m, kitchen and dining 4 x 5 m, living room 3.5 x 7 m
// opening on the yard. Upper: the front couple's room 4.5 x 4 m with a dressing nook 2 x 2 m and its
// shower room 2.5 x 2 m, the back couple's room 3.5 x 5 m and its shower room 3.5 x 2 m, the landing.
//
// Frame as the homesteads': the street is west, the door in the west wall, x the distance from the
// street, z along it. The side walls of the house are the party walls (the plot's shell); the
// gardens' edges are OPEN (`open_shell`): the yards behind a terrace are one green, each plot's
// north line marked by a mowing strip, the street edge a 0.9 m front garden wall with the gate.
// Every bedroom meets England's space standard inside its walls and every room is reached, lit and
// found by the game (crates/humanity-ship/src/home_program_tests.rs).
//
// Materials: 1 = steel (the shell), 2 = concrete, 3 = wood, 4 = glass, 9 = steel balustrade.
